# Flashable firmware images are build artifacts — publish via GitHub Releases, not git
*.trx
*.w

# OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp

# Local-only AI-agent context (references the maintainer's private environment)
CLAUDE.md
CLAUDE.local.md
.claude/
.mailmap
.vscode

# Python bytecode (build-scripts helpers)
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Flashable firmware images and their checksum lists are BUILD ARTIFACTS and are
# published as GitHub Release assets, which live outside the git repo. They were
# committed under releases/ until 2026-08-11 (~7.5 GB of blob history, ~830 MB
# packed) purely for file-tree visibility; nothing consumed them - the router's
# update check reads updates/manifest_3006.txt, and the release workflow attaches
# assets from the clean-room build artifacts.
# releases/latest.json IS still tracked: refresh_manifest.py regenerates it and
# the publish workflow commits it.
releases/**/*.pkgtb
releases/**/SHA256SUMS*.txt

# build-lab/ -- the local measurement harness for build-system changes.
#
# The METHOD and the VERDICTS are tracked (README.md, PROTOCOL.md with its
# results ledger, nondeterministic.txt, the scripts, and each session's
# REPORT.md + digest .env files -- about 150 KB). Those are the documented
# proof that a change to the build was safe, and they are worth more later
# than they are now.
#
# The BULK EVIDENCE is not tracked: full build logs run ~4.75 MB each and the
# staged-fs hash dumps ~330 KB per variant, so a single A/B session is ~13 MB
# of regenerable output. Same reasoning as releases/ above -- this repo already
# carried ~7.5 GB of build artifacts once and does not need to again.
#
# To ignore the harness entirely instead, replace this whole block with:
#   build-lab/
# but first move nondeterministic.txt somewhere tracked -- the promoted
# single-pass logic in build-scripts/_reaper_build_lib.sh refers to that
# finding, and an unexplained exclusion list is a place to hide a defect.
build-lab/RESULTS/**/build.log
build-lab/RESULTS/**/build.log.gz
build-lab/RESULTS/**/console.log
build-lab/RESULTS/**/console.log.gz
build-lab/RESULTS/**/stagedfs-hashes-*.txt
build-lab/RESULTS/**/stagedfs-inventory-*.txt
build-lab/RESULTS/**/.engine-backup-*/
# nondet-files-<MODEL>-<VARIANT>/ is deliberately NOT ignored. Those are ~9 KB
# per variant and are the primary evidence for the five-file irreproducibility
# claim -- the actual build_time / motd / image_version / modules.dep captures
# and the libshared.so ELF fingerprint. The claim justifies excluding files from
# the equality proof, so the evidence for it belongs in the repo.
